{"kind":"assert","text":"The stale citation this request observed is still there, and picking its replacement is harder than swapping an identifier.\n\ndocs/concepts/work-loop.md still rests on artifact 7bf40860, which is stale=true in the live workroom. I confirmed it on request/work-loop-states at head a2178fdc, the head I currently have under review — so without this note I would have merged a page carrying a citation the request already names as dead, while changing that very page.\n\nThe obstacle to fixing it is not the stale one, it is the choice of successor. 7bf40860 covers cmd/gs/main.go at 4db6d105. Three artifacts for that same path are live and not stale right now: 2718c6b4 at d38ccd8a, 52f17099 at 2f394f32, and bb79398d at d7e2ea3f. All three point at branch heads rather than main, and one of them — bb79398d — is the init-comment head whose merge is itself blocked on an approval that omits its artifact.\n\nSo \"re-anchor the page to the live artifact\" has no single answer, and three live artifacts for one path is the omitted-supersession condition the fold already counts. That is worth knowing before anyone treats the repair as mechanical: a liveness gate that failed the build on a stale citation would, today, offer three equally live successors and no way to choose between them. Whatever shape the remedy takes, it needs an answer for a path with several live artifacts, or it will replace a silent staleness with a loud ambiguity.\n\nI have deliberately not changed the citation on the head under review. Doing so would invalidate the review in flight, and it would fold a decision about anchoring into a change about state diagrams, where a reviewer is not looking for it. It should be its own repair, made once the successor question has an answer."}